{
  "_notes": [
    "Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles [Data East, 1991]",
    "2026-02-14 added by Tom Collins <tom@scorbit.io>",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E48 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum stored at 0x1EFE (checksum8_sum,",
    "the Whitestar form: not complemented). Measured on tmnt_200 from 845 live-RAM samples across",
    "two operator-menu sessions: Free Play 0 -> 1 at 0x1E04 moved 0x1EFE by 1, Balls Per Game",
    "3 -> 5 -> 3 at 0x1E0D moved it by 2 and back. A write that changes an adjustment without",
    "updating 0x1EFE is discarded at the next boot: the ROM resets the block to factory, which is",
    "how Free Play set by an external writer kept reverting. 0x1EFF counts menu changes.",
    "0x1DDF is the ROM's 'free play in effect' working flag: cleared while the operator menu is",
    "open and re-derived from 0x1E04 on leaving it and at boot. Data East resets the machine when",
    "the operator menu is exited, so a change to 0x1E04 made from outside the menu takes effect at",
    "the next boot rather than immediately.",
    "Adjustments 0x1E00-0x1E48 are protected by a plain 8-bit sum (complement false) at 0x1EFE; see README.md in maps/dataeast."
  ],
